{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '272,365p' docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html\"","aggregated_output":"<p>开题理由是 D184 定的四类，D236 把主驱动量扩到产品节点，所以写成五类。判两件事，互不顶替：这是谁的问题（标的还是主题）；为什么值得开（开题理由）。</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap wide\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>类</th><th>开题理由</th><th>标的或主题</th><th>问什么</th><th>量还是事件</th><th>期间和到期</th><th>核对材料 <code>settled_by</code></th><th>出处</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>A</b> 主驱动量</td><td><code>main_driver</code></td><td>标的</td><td>承载公司价值的那个年度量，不管公司指不指引：撑起业务的分部收入、毛利率、资本开支；跨行业如银行的净利息收入、零售商的同店销售、公用事业的费率基数、航空公司的燃油成本（当它是争论焦点时）。不是每一行报表数</td><td>量，五档</td><td>公司财年的今年或明年；到期日是这个数的发布日</td><td>公布这个数的公开材料，通常是年报</td><td>D184：<code>settled_by</code> 是 \"the public material that resolves it\"；PRD 06 梯子第 5 条</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>B</b> 主产品节点</td><td><code>main_driver</code></td><td>标的</td><td>承载公司价值的那一代产品哪天走到能带来收入的那一步（通常是开始出货）；发布、送样是它的证据，只有会分别下注的里程碑（新药的三期数据和获批）各一题<span class=\"src\">D248 第 3 条</span></td><td>事件，五档，或是非两档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 1 条</span></td><td>能判出结果的那天</td><td>公司公告、发货确认</td><td>D236</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>C</b> 约束性义务</td><td><code>binding_obligation</code></td><td>标的</td><td>公司以自己名义承担的：为别人的债务、租约或收入担保或提供信用支持；借钱给别人；承诺购买（向别人买产能或服务也算）；为客户的产能或收入兜底；或写明规模、尚未完成的入股或收购<span class=\"src\">D236；收购按 D243 第 7 条</span>。规模要大到能改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险才开；够不上的单笔入股、收购、租约、授信不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判<span class=\"src\">D248 第 6 条</span>。不算：自己借钱、自己的租约、已完成或没写规模的投资。D239 选定的 role-v29 原文：\"Its own borrowing, its own leases and a completed or unsized investment are not obligations\"；D238 的记录写作 \"the company's own borrowing and leases and a completed or unsized stake do not\"</td><td>还没签：是非两档。已经承担（一笔或一个计划）：金额，五档</td><td>检查日最多在文章后 18 个月<span class=\"src\">D185</span>；已承担的按下一份年报</td><td>签约公告、年报承诺附注</td><td>D184、D185、D210、D236、D238、D243</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>D</b> 共同量</td><td><code>shared_quantity</code><span class=\"src\">D191、D243 第 2 条</span>；现行提示词和代码还叫 <code>industry_aggregate</code>，按这一页改</td><td>主题</td><td>任何一家公司之外、好几家都会受它影响的量或价格：几家公司的合计（云厂商资本开支）、价格（内存合约价、油价）、利率。同一总量的另一种人群、另一种说法是这个量的证据</td><td>量，五档</td><td>自然年的今年或明年。同一个量、同一年只有一个问题，由代码按\"主题＋量＋期间\"判<span class=\"src\">D197</span>；量的类别是 <code>other</code> 的不算</td><td>几家公司年报、统计发布、官方决定</td><td>D184、D191、D197、D243；PRD 06</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>E</b> 政策阶段</td><td><code>policy_stage</code></td><td>问的是一家公司的收入、利润、份额或产品进度，算标的，即使由政策驱动；问的是世界上的事（许可制度、利率、合计支出），算主题。D184 采纳的 role-v12 原文：\"A question about a company's revenue, profit, share or product progress is an asset thesis; put its ticker in object, even when policy or macroeconomics drives it\"</td><td>一个政策或监管过程到了哪一步，写明谁说了算</td><td>事件，五档或两档</td><td>能判出那一步的那天。文章没写日期的待决监管事项，用本财年末（role-v12 原文：\"A pending regulatory decision may lack a date; use the current fiscal year-end as its due date\"）；这个日期是研究员定的检查日，要标明<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 1 条</span></td><td>官方决定、公报</td><td>D184</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n<p>例子（跨行业）：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>A：</b>NVIDIA FY2027 数据中心收入；一家地区银行 FY2026 净利息收入；一家公用事业公司 2027 年费率基数。</li>\n<li><b>B：</b>下一代机架系统能否在 2027 年底前开始出货；一家车企的新平台能否在 2026 年内开始交付。</li>\n<li><b>C：</b>NVIDIA 为云客户产能兜底的义务在 FY2027 年报达到多少；一家保险公司是否在 2027 年中前为合资公司 5 亿美元债务签署担保。</li>\n<li><b>D：</b>五家最大云厂商 2026 年合计资本开支；2027 年 DRAM 合约价相对 2026 年的变化、美联储 2026 年最后一次会议后的利率上限。</li>\n<li><b>E：</b>中国是否在 2027-01-31 前正式批准本国公司进口 H200；美国是否在某日前对某类芯片实行出口许可。这两题问的是许可这件世界上的事，所以是主题，role-v12 原文的例子就是 \"licensing\"。一个监管决定对一家公司收入或产品进度的影响，问成那家公司的量或产品节点时，是标的问题（同一句原文）。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>五类之外的东西去哪</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>七类驱动不是问题类型。</b>它们是一条陈述为什么重要的理由，用来判分量和归档。D208 设计的\"每家公司种下的驱动问题\"由分析员开始覆盖时写好，不从文章里开；还没建。</li>\n<li><b>别家公司自己的量</b>（对手的份额、客户的资本开支）：D187 定了\"任何公司自己的量是那家公司的问题，私营公司也算\"，但还没实现，要先在覆盖名单里加私营公司这一类。D155 定了\"公司清单可以作为初始参考，但清单外不能忽略\"。现行代码在匹配时跳过名单外的对象<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 Step 4</span>。所以抽取照常可以提这样的问题，它要过第 4 节的测试；名单外的现在会被匹配跳过，这不算抽取错。</li>\n<li><b>宏观量</b>（利率、通胀）：按 D 类共同量开题<span class=\"src\">D243 第 2 条</span>。只来自一篇纯宏观文章时，只有主题在名单上才开<span class=\"src\">D191 第 3 条</span>。宏观对每家公司的正负，在判断那家公司时读主题块决定<span class=\"src\">D191 第 1 条、D195</span>。</li>\n<li><b>开题理由是封闭的</b><span class=\"src\">D184</span>：一件事属不属于五类之一，按上表逐条看，比如一个监管决定看它是不是 E 类。哪一类都不属于的不开；它是不是证据、挂到哪，照第 5 节和归档规则。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>问题怎么写：PRD 06 的梯子规则，不重写</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>一个问题只问一个量的一个期间，或一件事；能各自朝相反方向走、而且分析员会分别下注的部分要分开<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 3 条；\"分别下注\"是 D248 加的，PRD 06 签字后更新</span>，分开的每一题都要过第 4 节的测试。</li>\n<li>写成问句，不写成断言<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 Rationale</span>。</li>\n<li>结果档可核对、不重叠、不留缝，到期恰好一档成立；中间一档写明和什么比；\"小幅\"\"部分\"这种不能核对的说法不用，部分状态写成单独一档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 2 条</span>。标的问题的档描述业务结果；主题问题的档只写结局，不写好坏<span class=\"src\">PRD 06、D186</span>。</li>\n<li>到期日：量是它的发布日；事件是能判出结果的那天。公司的量用公司财年，别的用自然年，只开今年和明年<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 5 条；约束性义务例外，D185</span>。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2 id=\"opening\"><span class=\"num\">4</span>开题标准</h2>\n<blockquote><p><b>一个问题值得单独追，要同时满足三件事：它的答案可能改变仓位；能在一个日期用公开材料判出落在哪一档；库里没有问题在问同一件事。</b>开多少个是判断的结果，不是目标<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6；评审 §1</span>。</p>\n<p>颗粒度按一个高端对冲基金分析员：只有会单独下注的大事开题，鸡毛蒜皮不开题（它的陈述留不留照第 5 节判）；同一个赌注的几种说法是一题，截止日、里程碑、财年和日历年各按本节\"同一题、续期，还是另一题\"里的那一条判<span class=\"src\">D248</span>。</p>\n<p>另有一条前提：新问题要有独立的投资判断；一个新产品、一个新数字、一个更窄的范围，单凭这些不开<span class=\"src\">D201</span>。</p></blockquote>\n\n<h3>四个测试<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6</span></h3>\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><b>值得追</b>写得出\"这个结果会改变哪项收入、利润、现金或信用风险、竞争位置\"吗？写不出就留作证据，不开题。\"数字很大\"不算理由。单笔交易、产品、项目，规模够不上改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险的，不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判<span class=\"src\">D248 第 6 条：问的就是小交易、小产品</span>；这一测试的其余理由（包括竞争位置）不变。</li>\n<li><b>独立意义</b>能写出两个情景吗：其他问题的答案不变，只有这一题相反，而对业务的判断确实不同？写不出就优先作为证据<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 3、8 条</span>。评审里的一个判例：NVIDIA FY2027 总收入题判为数据中心收入题的证据，理由是\"该段明确说主要增长来自数据中心，未提出独立的其他业务争论\"。这是对那一段材料的判断，别的材料要逐个判。</li>\n<li><b>能核对</b>有一个日期和一份公开材料能把答案放进事先固定的档吗？没有就重写问题。到期没有材料记\"未能判定\"，不算错。</li>\n<li><b>不是重复</b>和已有问题比，只是预测值、措辞、来源、方向或同一总量的另一种口径不同，最终核对的是同一个结果吗？是就是同一题。抽取看不到库<span class=\"src\">D211</span>，这一条在抽取时只对同一篇文章里提出的几个问题判；和库里的比由匹配做。</li>\n</ol>\n<p>另外三条写法检查<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 1、5、6 条</span>。没过的问题不能照原样开，要重写；重写不了就不开，材料作证据。</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>原文支持：</b>主体、量或事件、时间依据都能在原文找到。原文没给日期、而规则允许研究员定检查日的，用那个日期并标明：没写日期的待决监管事项用本财年末（第 3 节 E 类）；还没签的约束性义务用文章后 18 个月以内能核对签约的那天<span class=\"src\">D185、D210</span>。不把\"拟议\"\"预计\"写成\"已签\"\"已完成\"。</li>\n<li><b>口径完整：</b>算谁、不算谁、算什么写清楚；支出、融资、担保、订单、收入不混。</li>\n<li><b>时间正确：</b>原文支持这个期间，不把几年的平均写成今年。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>不开的<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6 的清单</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap mid\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>不开</th><th>出处</th><th>它变成什么</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>季度数字和季度指引</td><td>第 1 版 §6；PRD 06 梯子第 6 条</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n<tr><td>同一段指引里的每一行（\"费用率、税率是模型输入，不是争论\"）</td><td>第 1 版 §6</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n<tr><td>没日期的\"护城河\"\"战略\"</td><td>第 1 版 §6</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n<tr><td>高管任免、股东投票、回购授权；章程</td><td>第 1 版 §6；章程出自 D239 选定的 role-v29 原文（\"executive appointments, shareholder votes or bylaws\"）</td><td>证据或不留</td></tr>\n<tr><td>例行诉讼程序</td><td>第 1 版 §6</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n<tr><td>客户的部署计划（\"它是供应商需求和产品问题的证据，除非改变供应商自己的现金或信用风险\"）</td><td>第 1 版 §6</td><td>证据；改变公司自己的现金或信用风险时按 C 类判</td></tr>\n<tr><td>以约束性义务为理由开：公司自己借钱、自己的租约、已完成或没写规模的投资。它们不是约束性义务；对别的问题仍可以是证据，或按别的开题理由判</td><td>D236、D238</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n<tr><td>把远期年度预测改装成事件</td><td>第 1 版 §6</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n<tr><td>后年及以后的年度量（约束性义务除外）</td><td>PRD 06 梯子第 5 条；D185</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n<tr><td>同一个量的另一个估计、另一种口径、另一个来源</td><td>第 1 版 §6 测试 4</td><td>那个已开问题的证据，由匹配并入</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n<h3>同一题、续期，还是另一题：匹配这一步的事，抽取不判库里的</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>总规则：</b>同一个结果能判掉两题，就是同一题；答案能分开走、而且分析员会分别下注的，才是另一题<span class=\"src\">D248</span>。</li>\n<li><b>同一题：</b>同一个结果能同时判两个问题。另一个估计、来源、措辞、方向<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6 测试 4</span>；同一总量的另一种人群或代用口径（D190 碰撞裁决提示 collision-v1：\"another population or proxy of one aggregate\"；D197 引的 role-v12 原文：\"another population or another wording of the same aggregate is evidence to the shown aggregate thesis\"）。候选并进已开问题，用它的结果档和到期日<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span>。只有以共同量理由开题、带量的候选由代码自动判，其余是匹配和碰撞裁决的判断。</li>\n<li><b>同一个计划的几种说法</b>（担保、融资承诺、信用支持……），最后核对的是同一个数，是一题<span class=\"src\">D248 第 1 条</span>。</li>\n<li><b>同一件事的不同截止日：</b>早的那题开着时，晚的截止日是它的证据，不另开；早的到期没有结果、事情还在追，系统开下一个截止日的续期题，带上并进来的证据，不等新文章<span class=\"src\">D248 第 2 条</span>。</li>\n<li><b>同一代产品的几个里程碑：</b>一题，问能带来收入的那一步（通常是开始出货）；送样、发布作证据；会分别下注的里程碑（新药的三期数据和获批）各一题<span class=\"src\">D248 第 3 条</span>。</li>\n<li><b>公司自己的量：</b>只按财年开题；按日历年的估计是财年那题的证据，两种年份差得多时分量低一点<span class=\"src\">D248 第 4 条；PRD 06 梯子第 5 条</span>。</li>\n<li><b>身份：</b>事件和政策题里模型写的期间起点，不拿来挡合并；对象、事件、截止日照旧核对<span class=\"src\">D248 第 5 条</span>。</li>\n<li><b>续期：</b>同一个量或同一串事件的下一个期间<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 Succession、D190</span>。</li>\n<li><b>另一题：</b>同一件事里答案能分开走、分析员会分别下注的：有自己驱动的组成部分；同一笔交易或同一份附注里两个各自会变、分别盯着的数；另一件事<span class=\"src\">D190 碰撞裁决的四种；D248 第 1 条收窄了\"担保和融资\"</span>。</li>\n<li><b>约束性义务：</b>\"一笔或一个计划\"一题<span class=\"src\">D210</span>；一笔交易是不是某个已按金额开题的计划的一部分，由匹配判，是就并入<span class=\"src\">D248 第 1 条</span>。还没签的单笔交易是\"签不签\"的是非题，照旧可以开，不并进计划的金额题<span class=\"src\">D210；PRD 06；D248 未改</span>。</li>\n<li><b>共同量：</b>以共同量理由开题、带量的候选（量的类别是 <code>other</code> 的不算），由代码按\"主题＋量＋期间\"判同一题；政策阶段和别的事件保留按事件判的身份；不带这个开题理由的主题量由模型判<span class=\"src\">D197</span>。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>谁判，谁查</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap mid\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>内容</th><th>谁</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>测试 1–3、同一篇文章里的测试 4、属于哪一类、问题怎么写</td><td>抽取的模型（判断）</td></tr>\n<tr><td>结果档形状、期间是真日期、到期在文章之后、季度数、年限、约束性义务 18 个月、<code>settled_by</code> 不为空</td><td>代码：只查形状，不判重要性<span class=\"src\">D154、D155、D184</span></td></tr>\n<tr><td>和库里的同一题、续期、另一题</td><td>匹配（Jev）和碰撞裁决<span class=\"src\">D190</span>；共同量由代码<span class=\"src\">D197</span></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-system.txt | sed -n '1,13p;42,58p;85,135p'; nl -ba clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-closing.txt | tail -n 7; nl -ba clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-schema.json | sed -n '1,115p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-system.txt | sed -n '1,13p;42,58p;85,135p'; nl -ba clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-closing.txt | tail -n 7; nl -ba clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-schema.json | sed -n '1,115p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\tROLE\n     2\t\n     3\tYou are a senior hedge-fund analyst reading one source item for the company in scope (current_entity); \"the company\" below is that\n     4\tcompany. The research already tracked for it is listed in open_theses. Your first job is evidence: decide by the rules below which\n     5\tstatements in the item are material, then link each one to every thesis it informs: an open thesis that covers it, a new thesis you\n     6\tpropose, or both. Your second job is new theses: the important research questions this item raises that no open thesis\n     7\tcovers. Every new thesis comes with evidence from this item. A material statement that no open thesis covers and that is not\n     8\titself a big matter (section 3) is returned with empty links: code keeps it in the company's record without links and links it\n     9\twhen a thesis that covers it opens. Never open a thesis only to give a statement a home.\n    10\t\n    11\tINPUT\n    12\t\n    13\t- current_entity and company_tags: the company in scope and the companies the item is tagged with. Code assigns the entity; do not\n    42\t  of the closing check at the end of this request rejects it; a row's \"it does not cover\" clause sends the statement back to that test\n    43\t  and keeps it only where the row says so. Most of an item is background, but a page with eight statements that pass yields eight\n    44\t  evidence items, not a selection.\n    45\t\n    46\t2. LINK EACH STATEMENT TO ITS THESES\n    47\t\n    48\t- EXISTING: if an open thesis covers the statement, link it to that thesis's exact supplied ID, including contrary facts. Do not\n    49\t  return or rename the thesis's description.\n    50\t- NEW: if the statement raises a research question that merits separate tracking and no open or newly proposed thesis covers it,\n    51\t  propose a thesis (section 3) and link the statement to it.\n    52\t- NO THESIS YET: if no open or newly proposed thesis covers a statement you judge material, and the matter is not big enough by\n    53\t  its own scale to merit a thesis (section 3), return it with empty links; it is kept without links.\n    54\t- CONDITION: a statement of the company's own financial figures (a reported result or balance, its guidance, or a named party's\n    55\t  or consensus estimate) lists its useful figures in figures. Its results, guidance and estimates, margins included, inform an open thesis about its revenue or earnings\n    56\t  path when they bear on that path; a different period is not on its own a reason to leave them unlinked. When no open or new\n    57\t  thesis covers it, its links stay empty. A figure is useful when it can change what an analyst\n    58\t  expects of the company's revenue, profitability, funding or credit risk, or competitive position: a retailer's quarterly\n    85\t3. WHEN TO PROPOSE A NEW THESIS\n    86\t\n    87\tA thesis is a question a senior analyst would hold a card for: its answer could change a position because it could change the\n    88\tcompany's revenue, profit, cash or credit risk, or competitive position in a way you can name; public material will settle it on a\n    89\tdate; and no open thesis already asks it. A thesis asks one quantity for one period, or one event. It opens for one of five reasons, a closed set; a matter that fits none of them is\n    90\tevidence, kept and linked to the theses it informs or left unlinked, never a thesis:\n    91\t- main_driver: the annual quantity that carries the company's value, for its current or next fiscal year, whether or not the company\n    92\t  guides it: the revenue of the segment that carries the business, or the gross margin (\"the bank's net interest income this fiscal\n    93\t  year\"; \"the retailer's same-store sales growth next fiscal year\"; an airline's fuel cost only when it is the focus of debate). It\n    94\t  is not every line of the statements. The material that publishes the figure settles it, usually the annual report, on its release\n    95\t  date.\n    96\t- product_node: when the generation of the main product that carries the company's value reaches the step that brings revenue,\n    97\t  usually first shipments; announcements and samples are its evidence, and only milestones an analyst bets on separately (a drug's\n    98\t  trial result and its approval) are separate theses (\"will the carmaker's new platform start deliveries in 2026?\";\n    99\t  \"will the drugmaker's next-generation inhaler, the product line that carries its value, reach pharmacies by mid-2027?\").\n   100\t- binding_obligation: an obligation the company takes on in its own name, large enough to change its revenue, profit, cash or credit\n   101\t  risk: guaranteeing, backing or giving credit support for another party's debt, lease, revenue or capacity, lending to it,\n   102\t  committing to buy capacity or services, or a sized stake or acquisition not yet completed. One already undertaken is tracked by its\n   103\t  amount at the next annual report; one not yet signed by whether it is signed by a check date within 18 months of the item (\"how much will the\n   104\t  utility have guaranteed for its project companies' loans at its next annual report?\"; \"will the retailer sign a guarantee for its\n   105\t  franchisees' leases, large enough to change its credit risk, by the check date?\"). Its own borrowing or leases and a completed\n   106\t  or unsized investment are not obligations.\n   107\t- shared_quantity: a quantity or price outside any one company that several companies depend on, for this or next calendar year:\n   108\t  several companies' combined output or spending, a contract price, an interest rate (\"the largest container lines' combined capacity\n   109\t  added in 2026\"; \"next year's average contract price of a raw material\"). Another population or wording of the same aggregate is\n   110\t  evidence for it.\n   111\t- policy_stage: the step a policy or regulatory process reaches, naming who decides (\"will the regulator approve the drug for a second\n   112\t  indication?\"; \"will the government require licences for the product's exports by a date?\").\n   113\t\n   114\t- Open only matters an analyst would bet on separately; small matters open no thesis and their statements are kept as evidence. A\n   115\t  customer's deployment plan is evidence for the company's demand and product theses, unless it changes the company's own cash or\n   116\t  credit risk, which is judged as an obligation.\n   117\t- Give the date the item supports. When it gives none, use the date the reason fixes and say how it was set: an obligation already\n   118\t  undertaken, its next annual report; an unsigned obligation, a check date within 18 months of the item; a pending regulatory\n   119\t  decision, the current fiscal year-end. A shared quantity takes its release date and a product event the date its outcome can be\n   120\t  checked, only when the item supports one. A question no date can settle is rewritten or not opened.\n   121\t- Do not open a thesis about: an executive appointment or organisational change; the company's own borrowing or leases as an\n   122\t  obligation; a buyback authorisation or dividend declaration; a quarter's figures or guidance, or the level, growth, margin or guidance of a\n   123\t  financial measure that is not a main_driver quantity, on its own; an undated moat or strategy; a feature, content or software update, price point, regional service or variant of a\n   124\t  product already on sale; another estimate, source or wording of what an open thesis tracks; an annual quantity after next year (an\n   125\t  obligation excepted); shareholder votes, bylaws or routine litigation procedure. Their statements are evidence for the theses they\n   126\t  inform, or left unlinked.\n   127\t- Before proposing a new thesis, name its reason (opens_as), the public material that will settle it (settled_by), and the closest\n   128\t  open thesis with why an analyst would bet on the two separately because their answers can move apart; with no open thesis, say so.\n   129\t  If the two cannot move apart, link the evidence to every open thesis it informs instead.\n   130\t\n   131\tCounterexamples:\n   132\t\n   133\t- \"The company's outlook is interesting\" or \"the industry may change\" is too vague: it names no outcome later evidence can inform.\n   134\t- If an open thesis tracks sales growth, a revised sales forecast is evidence for it; do not open a second thesis to repeat it.\n   135\t- A customer expanding capacity informs demand; it is not a thesis of its own, and not a claim that the supplier has received orders.\n    10\t- the same fact said again in other words within this item: one deal, hire, programme or reported measure told in several sentences, with its terms, figures and growth rates, is one evidence item; keep the fuller wording (\"a $2 billion order for 120 stores in 15 countries over three years\"; \"cloud revenue of $8 billion, up 30% on the year and 6% on the quarter, 40% of the total\"); a deal one party signs under a wider programme, with its own amount or capacity, is its own evidence item, and a fact another outlet reported before is not a repeat within this item;\n    11\t- company boilerplate, bylines, forward-looking-statement text.\n    12\tA report and another party's denial or confirmation of it are two items, each kept only if it passes the test above; an estimate stays apart from any valuation drawn from it, and the valuation is not kept; one party's statement keeps its own planned or rumoured details.\n    13\tReturn only the evidence items you keep.\n    14\tThen check the theses and links. A new thesis that asks the same underlying question, about the same subject and scope, as an open thesis or another new thesis is not proposed: link its evidence to that thesis. A new thesis needs at least one kept evidence item, and a vague or noisy topic with no outcome to watch is not proposed. Each kept evidence item links to every thesis it informs and to no thesis its own relevance says it does not inform.\n    15\tFor each new thesis, check its opens_as, settled_by, closest_open_thesis and why_a_separate_bet: drop the thesis if it fits none of the five reasons in section 3, if no public material will settle it on a date, if an open thesis exists and its answer cannot move apart from it, or if it falls under a 'do not open' item in section 3; then link its evidence to every open thesis it informs, or leave it without links.\n    16\tAn item whose only home would be a new thesis that is not a big matter is returned with empty links and kept without links; an item an open thesis covers is linked there, not left without links. Then read back each statement you return with empty links that states the company's own figures: return it only if a figure can change what an analyst expects of the company's revenue, profitability, funding or credit risk, or competitive position; for example, a cash-rich company's balance or cash flow that the item ties to nothing usually cannot; return only what passes.\n     1\t{\n     2\t \"type\": \"object\",\n     3\t \"additionalProperties\": false,\n     4\t \"required\": [\n     5\t  \"new_theses\",\n     6\t  \"evidence\"\n     7\t ],\n     8\t \"properties\": {\n     9\t  \"new_theses\": {\n    10\t   \"type\": \"array\",\n    11\t   \"description\": \"New thesis proposals, each referenced by at least one evidence link.\",\n    12\t   \"items\": {\n    13\t    \"type\": \"object\",\n    14\t    \"additionalProperties\": false,\n    15\t    \"required\": [\n    16\t     \"local_id\",\n    17\t     \"description\",\n    18\t     \"outcome\",\n    19\t     \"period\",\n    20\t     \"opens_as\",\n    21\t     \"settled_by\",\n    22\t     \"closest_open_thesis\",\n    23\t     \"why_a_separate_bet\"\n    24\t    ],\n    25\t    \"properties\": {\n    26\t     \"local_id\": {\n    27\t      \"type\": \"string\",\n    28\t      \"description\": \"Local reference for this new thesis in the answer; not a database ID.\"\n    29\t     },\n    30\t     \"description\": {\n    31\t      \"type\": \"string\",\n    32\t      \"description\": \"The proposed research question, stated clearly.\"\n    33\t     },\n    34\t     \"outcome\": {\n    35\t      \"type\": \"string\",\n    36\t      \"description\": \"The outcome or event being tracked by this thesis.\"\n    37\t     },\n    38\t     \"period\": {\n    39\t      \"anyOf\": [\n    40\t       {\n    41\t        \"type\": \"string\"\n    42\t       },\n    43\t       {\n    44\t        \"type\": \"null\"\n    45\t       }\n    46\t      ],\n    47\t      \"description\": \"The period or check date that settles the thesis: the one the item supports, or the one its reason fixes (section 3), with how it was set.\"\n    48\t     },\n    49\t     \"opens_as\": {\n    50\t      \"type\": \"string\",\n    51\t      \"enum\": [\n    52\t       \"main_driver\",\n    53\t       \"product_node\",\n    54\t       \"binding_obligation\",\n    55\t       \"shared_quantity\",\n    56\t       \"policy_stage\"\n    57\t      ],\n    58\t      \"description\": \"The reason this thesis opens, one of the five in section 3.\"\n    59\t     },\n    60\t     \"settled_by\": {\n    61\t      \"type\": \"string\",\n    62\t      \"description\": \"The public material that will settle the answer on a date (a filing, an official decision, a shipment confirmation, a statistics release).\",\n    63\t      \"pattern\": \"\\\\S\"\n    64\t     },\n    65\t     \"closest_open_thesis\": {\n    66\t      \"anyOf\": [\n    67\t       {\n    68\t        \"type\": \"string\"\n    69\t       },\n    70\t       {\n    71\t        \"type\": \"null\"\n    72\t       }\n    73\t      ],\n    74\t      \"description\": \"Exact ID of the open thesis closest to this one; null when the open list is empty.\"\n    75\t     },\n    76\t     \"why_a_separate_bet\": {\n    77\t      \"type\": \"string\",\n    78\t      \"description\": \"Why an analyst would bet on this question separately from the closest open thesis: how their answers can move apart.\"\n    79\t     }\n    80\t    }\n    81\t   }\n    82\t  },\n    83\t  \"evidence\": {\n    84\t   \"type\": \"array\",\n    85\t   \"description\": \"Evidence statements extracted from this item, with their thesis links.\",\n    86\t   \"items\": {\n    87\t    \"type\": \"object\",\n    88\t    \"additionalProperties\": false,\n    89\t    \"required\": [\n    90\t     \"local_id\",\n    91\t     \"summary\",\n    92\t     \"source_passages\",\n    93\t     \"original_party\",\n    94\t     \"reporting_speaker\",\n    95\t     \"tier\",\n    96\t     \"statement_date\",\n    97\t     \"statement_date_text\",\n    98\t     \"evidence_period\",\n    99\t     \"links\",\n   100\t     \"figures\"\n   101\t    ],\n   102\t    \"properties\": {\n   103\t     \"local_id\": {\n   104\t      \"type\": \"string\",\n   105\t      \"description\": \"Local reference for this evidence in the answer; not a database ID.\"\n   106\t     },\n   107\t     \"summary\": {\n   108\t      \"type\": \"string\",\n   109\t      \"description\": \"Standalone faithful summary naming the actor and preserving relevant figures, periods and conditions.\"\n   110\t     },\n   111\t     \"source_passages\": {\n   112\t      \"type\": \"array\",\n   113\t      \"minItems\": 1,\n   114\t      \"description\": \"Contiguous verbatim passages from this source item that jointly support the summary; return each passage separately.\",\n   115\t      \"items\": {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"**The candidate reflects the signed standard’s main-driver category, but it is wider than the test Alex approved in D490, and it leaves two practical gaps: how to avoid duplicate questions and how to give an annual question a supported release date.** For example, “an airline’s fuel cost” is a valid example in the signed standard, but D490 asked about testing the company’s revenue and margin; the candidate also invites that fuel-cost question.\n\nThis is a read-only assessment of the text. It identifies possible model behavior, not measured results. I compared the system and closing files with `diff` and compared the schemas as parsed JSON. The schema changes only the reason description from four to five and adds `main_driver` to the enum.\n\n### Each changed sentence\n\nSources: [candidate system](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-system.txt:87), [candidate closing check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-closing.txt:14), [candidate schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-schema.json:49), [signed standard](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:272), and [D490](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:5571).\n\n| Change | Verdict | Source and reasoning |\n|---|---|---|\n| “It opens for one of **five** reasons, a closed set…” | **Consistent with the standard and D490’s test**, conditional on the fifth reason being scoped correctly. | §3 says “开题理由是封闭的” and lists five categories. D490 opens a test departure from D382/D384; those decisions still govern the adopted request. |\n| “**main_driver: the annual quantity that carries the company’s value, for its current or next fiscal year, whether or not the company guides it**…” | **Consistent with §3; keeps wider than D490’s stated test.** | Row A says “承载公司价值的那个年度量，不管公司指不指引” and “公司财年的今年或明年.” D490’s exact question was how to handle “营收和毛利率,” and the approved option was to test questions of that kind. “Annual quantity” also permits other measures. D490’s later summary says “company’s main numbers,” so the record itself is broader than its exact question; that breadth should not silently expand the test. |\n| “…**the revenue of the segment that carries the business, or the gross margin**…” | **Consistent**, subject to the separate-bet test. | Row A expressly names “撑起业务的分部收入、毛利率.” Section 4 adds “一个新数字、一个更窄的范围，单凭这些不开” and requires independently different business outcomes. A major segment is not automatically a second question beside total revenue. |\n| “**the bank’s net interest income this fiscal year; the retailer’s same-store sales growth next fiscal year; an airline’s fuel cost only when it is the focus of debate**” | **Consistent with the standard in substance; keeps wider than D490’s test.** | Row A names bank net interest income, retailer same-store sales and airline fuel cost when debated. The standard says same-store sales; the example specifies **growth**, which can describe the same outcome in another form and needs the duplicate check. Fuel cost and potentially same-store sales are outside the clearly stated revenue-and-margin test. |\n| “**It is not every line of the statements.**” | **Consistent.** | Row A: “不是每一行报表数.” Section 4 also rejects opening every line of guidance. |\n| “**The material that publishes the figure settles it, usually the annual report, on its release date.**” | **Consistent, but incomplete as an instruction for an unknown date.** | Row A: “公布这个数的公开材料，通常是年报”; “到期日是这个数的发布日.” The sentence identifies the kind of date but does not explain what to return when the item does not supply the release day. |\n| Revised do-not-open row: “**a quarter’s figures or guidance, or the level, growth, margin or guidance of a financial measure that is not a main_driver quantity, on its own**” | **Consistent with §3–4 as a general main-driver exception; keeps wider than D490’s stated test.** | §4 excludes “季度数字和季度指引” and every line of the same guidance; row A permits a qualifying annual main driver. Since `main_driver` is wider than revenue and margin, the exception is wider too. The qualifying “on its own” also leaves other opening reasons available, which is appropriate. |\n| Closing check: “**five reasons**” instead of four | **Consistent as bookkeeping; inherits the wider fifth reason.** | §3 has five categories; D490 permits the test exception. The remaining checks still require a public settlement, separate outcome and compliance with the do-not-open list. |\n| Schema description “**one of the five**” and enum addition `main_driver` | **Consistent as representation; inherits the same scope issue.** | Row A names `main_driver`. The enum makes the new answer expressible; it does not itself limit which measures qualify. |\n\nD382 says financial figures are conditions unless there is a reason that is the view; D384 excludes class A from the adopted clean path. D490 authorizes **testing** an exception, not adoption of the candidate. [D382 and D384](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4107).\n\n### Conflicts and tensions inside the request\n\n- **Role paragraph:** No direct contradiction. A main annual question can be an important question raised by an item, supported by evidence. “Never open a thesis only to give a statement a home” still rules out opening one merely because a figure appears.\n- **CONDITION:** No direct contradiction. A financial figure can be recorded as a condition and inform a revenue or earnings question; the fifth reason can also allow a qualifying annual question. The wording about an **open** thesis does not prohibit a new one: the next sentence explicitly says “open or new.”\n- **One quantity, one period:** No direct contradiction, but the growth example exposes an ambiguity. A level and its growth may be two ways to ask about the same result, rather than two separately bettable outcomes.\n- **Date rule:** There is a real instruction gap. The new reason says the figure’s release date settles it, but the general date paragraph does not list `main_driver` among the reasons whose date it fixes. It starts “Give the date the item supports” and ends by rejecting a question no date can settle. An item may identify FY revenue without giving its publication day; the schema does not supply that day.\n- **Another estimate, source or wording:** Compatible in principle. It prevents a revised forecast or another phrasing of an already tracked result from becoming another question. It does not explicitly show that **level versus growth** can be the same underlying result.\n- **Annual quantity after next year:** Compatible with “current or next fiscal year.” Both reject an annual main-driver question beyond that window. The request should not reinterpret a later-year forecast as a current-year forecast.\n- **`closest_open_thesis` and `why_a_separate_bet`:** Compatible and useful for an existing question. They require a reason the answers can move apart. They do not explicitly require the same independent-bet comparison **between two new questions**: the closing check checks same underlying question among new proposals, but its “cannot move apart” test names only an open thesis.\n- **Closing check on figures and conditions:** The instruction not to drop a reported figure merely because it was retold concerns *evidence*, not automatic question opening. The same-fact row combines a reported measure and its growth in one evidence item; it does not decide whether two research questions are independently meaningful. The final cash-flow check applies only to **unlinked company figures**; a figure linked to a newly opened question does not receive that particular check. The earlier general evidence test still applies. This makes the decision to open a question consequential for what survives.\n- **Closing check on reasons:** Changing four to five is internally consistent. It does not say that the new fifth reason replaces the other four.\n\n### Examples\n\nThe new examples use generic bank, retailer and airline descriptions. They name no covered company, product or number, and draw on several industries. Their measures are supported by row A, with the qualification that the retailer example changes “same-store sales” to “same-store sales **growth**.”\n\nThey fit the schema’s ability to express a question, outcome, period, reason and settling material, but **the examples themselves do not supply a release date or identify the public document**. They are measure examples, not complete valid output examples. The airline example agrees with the standard but exceeds the clearly stated revenue-and-margin test.\n\n### Specific risks and smallest wording changes\n\nThese are risks in how the request can be read, not claims that the model will make these mistakes.\n\n**(a) Every statement line, including EPS, net income, cash flow or a small segment.** The limiting words are “the annual quantity that carries the company’s value,” “not every line” and “only matters an analyst would bet on separately.” They make indiscriminate opening contrary to the text, but “annual quantity” leaves the model to decide whether any of those measures carries value. The fuel-cost example makes the category visibly broader than revenue and margin.\n\nFor the D490 test, the smallest scope correction is to replace **“the annual quantity”** with **“the company’s annual revenue or margin”**, and remove or replace examples outside that scope. Retain the existing importance and separate-bet tests. This is a restriction to the approved test, not a claim that the signed standard excludes other main drivers.\n\n**(b) A quarter or a year after next fiscal year.** The explicit “current or next fiscal year,” quarter exclusion and “annual quantity after next year” oppose both. No additional prohibition is needed. A missing fiscal year is a separate problem: the model should not infer one from a quarterly figure or a distant forecast.\n\n**(c) Two questions for level and growth, or total and main segment.** “Same-store sales growth” alongside “revenue” and “gross margin,” combined with “one quantity,” can make the same result look like two different measures. A main segment is explicitly eligible, while the separate-bet check against **new** questions is less explicit than against open ones.\n\nThe smallest sourced clarification is: **“Compare each proposed question with open and other proposed questions: if the same result settles both, keep one; separate them only if their answers can move apart and an analyst would bet on them separately.”** This follows §4’s “同一个结果能判掉两题，就是同一题” and its separate-bet test. It does **not** categorically merge total and segment: §4 says to judge the actual material, and a segment can have independent drivers.\n\n**(d) Another company’s figures.** For this new reason, “the company” is defined as `current_entity`, and “the company’s value” points back to it. The condition field also excludes other companies’ figures. Those words constrain the new category; an inadvertent opening remains possible because evidence can describe another party, but the candidate does not instruct it. A minimal clarification, if needed, is **“the current entity’s own annual revenue or margin.”** Note that the signed standard separately permits proposing another company’s own question subject to its tests; this candidate’s current-entity scope is narrower, so do not generalize this restriction beyond the requested test.\n\n**(e) The other four reasons stop opening.** There is no explicit instruction to stop them: the five reasons are alternatives and all four remain in the schema. The broad financial prohibition applies to a financial measure **on its own**, while the other categories have their own criteria. A model could nevertheless overapply that row to an obligation or shared quantity. The smallest clarification is **“This financial-figure row does not exclude a matter that independently meets another reason.”** That restates the existing closed-set structure rather than adding a new opening reason.\n\n### What is missing to write the question\n\n- **Measure and scope:** The schema has `description` and `outcome`, but neither explicitly asks for the exact measure and scope—such as total revenue versus a named segment, or which margin. Section 4 requires “算谁、不算谁、算什么写清楚.” The answer can express this, but the new instruction does not make the distinction explicit.\n- **Fiscal year:** The new reason requires current or next fiscal year, and `period` can carry it. It does not tell the model what to do if the source does not identify a supported fiscal year. Section 4 requires the subject, measure and time to be supported by the source; it should not invent one.\n- **Settling material:** Present: `settled_by` requires public material, and the new sentence says the publication of the figure, usually the annual report. The document should actually publish the specified measure and scope.\n- **Date:** The *kind* of date is present—the figure’s release date—but a supported actual day may be absent. The schema’s `period` allows null and combines period with check date; `settled_by` is only a string. The request does not resolve how to supply an unknown future release date without inventing it. Section 4 requires a date and public material, and permits an analyst-set date only in the specified cases; it does not provide that fallback for the annual main driver."}}
